{"id": "EUVD-2026-45572", "enisaUuid": "9c805d8a-9e14-37ea-b172-a89a0c67f9e7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nethtool: rss: fix indir_table and hkey leak on get_rxfh failure\n\nrss_prepare_get() allocates the indirection table and hash key buffer\nvia rss_get_data_alloc(), then calls ops->get_rxfh() to populate them.\nIf get_rxfh() fails, the function returns an error without freeing\nthe allocation.", "datePublished": "2026-07-19T14:56:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:42:52", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/14dbf22c397b799b3a80f63fc90c2fc0585bbeb3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/323faef6366349f57d4ad67d318a0c8906e360b3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/33d05c22d6f227c5ae171c46df2f6f8bf48047ea", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/80d95d92f828cfcace955d673637d944178b435f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/266297692f97008ca48bc311775c087c59bd7fe3"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9pm4-3wgp-cph8", "CVE-2026-63999"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07e69efe-dab6-3359-ae5a-6f338dc188a3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.24 <6.12.114"}, {"id": "186181cf-53d5-3447-b8b2-a5e7d14a0871", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5eb3fdc4b6281b29e830300c866a36d90442b1f0"}, {"id": "38524164-f28e-31e1-8ca4-f89b2d6c2bb1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f038a6a02d20859a3479293cbf172b0f14cbdd6 <266297692f97008ca48bc311775c087c59bd7fe3"}, {"id": "3885f567-8637-339e-81ee-4a2f970b0384", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f038a6a02d20859a3479293cbf172b0f14cbdd6 <33d05c22d6f227c5ae171c46df2f6f8bf48047ea"}, {"id": "3bd4a9b6-d52d-389c-9e97-d00f7bd99044", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "425b085c-6341-3b57-b376-91ba8e88f5ae", "prod